Microsoft Learn: Configure Azure App Service

Platform: Microsoft Learn
Module: Configure Azure App Service
Track: AZ-104 Microsoft Azure Administrator
Difficulty: Intermediate
Date: 2026

Objective

Learn how to deploy, configure, secure, monitor, and manage Azure App Service applications, including deployment slots, custom domains, backups, and application monitoring.

This module focused on managing Azure App Service as a Platform as a Service (PaaS) solution for hosting web applications, APIs, and backend services without managing the underlying infrastructure.

Step 1: Understanding Azure App Service

The module introduced Azure App Service as Microsoft's fully managed Platform as a Service (PaaS) offering for hosting web applications.

Azure App Service allows developers to deploy applications without managing:

Virtual Machines
Operating systems
Patching
Infrastructure maintenance
Supported workloads:
Web Applications
REST APIs
Backend Services
Mobile App Backends
Supported languages:
.NET
Java
Node.js
Python
PHP
Ruby
Benefits:
Rapid deployment
Built-in scaling
High availability
Integrated security
Simplified management

The module emphasized that App Service allows administrators to focus on applications rather than infrastructure.

Step 2: Creating an Azure App Service Application

The training covered creating a web application using Azure App Service.

Required components:
Component	Purpose
Subscription	Billing container
Resource Group	Resource organization
App Service Plan	Compute resources
Web App Name	Application identifier
Runtime Stack	Programming language
Example:
Resource Group:
RG-WebApp

App Service Plan:
ASP-Production

Web App:
contoso-webapp
Key lessons learned:
Every App Service requires an App Service Plan
Multiple applications can share the same App Service Plan
Runtime selection affects application compatibility
